    <string name="metric_decode_desc">(generatedTokens − 1) ÷ decode time. The per-token generation speed — the number most on-device comparisons turn on.</string>
    <string name="metric_decode_term">decode (generation rate)</string>
    <string name="metric_engine_diff_desc">· MNN: reads the engine\'s prefill_us / decode_us directly — pure compute time with no JNI callback or UI dispatch, comparable to the PERF lines in MnnLlmChat.
· Genie: streams text fragments rather than discrete tokens, so generatedTokens approximates the callback count.
· LiteRT-LM / llama.cpp: no per-stage timings are reported, so a wall-clock measurement is used — those numbers are naturally lower than pure compute rates.</string>
    <string name="metric_engine_diff_term">Engine measurement differences</string>
    <string name="metric_p50_desc">Median gap between consecutive token callbacks: how steady generation is. Lower is steadier.</string>
    <string name="metric_p50_term">p50 (median per-token time)</string>
    <string name="metric_prefill_desc">promptTokens ÷ prefill time. How fast the model reads the input; it matters more the longer the prompt is.</string>
    <string name="metric_prefill_term">prefill (input processing rate)</string>
    <string name="metric_tokens_desc">Input token count and generated token count for this turn.</string>
    <string name="metric_ttft_desc">From the generate() call to the first token callback. Excludes model load and template formatting. Uses the engine\'s own prefill time when it reports one (MNN\'s prefill_us), otherwise falls back to a wall-clock measurement.</string>
    <string name="metric_ttft_term">TTFT (first-token latency)</string>
    <string name="metric_wall_clock_note">For the same model, wall-clock numbers are lower than engine-reported ones, because the former also counts the per-token JNI callback and UI dispatch.</string>
